=== NOTES ===
Adoption deviation per the prompt's Blocked Path:

1. Vehicle nickname adoption was DROPPED. The current
   web/src/features/vehicles/pages/VehicleDetailPage.tsx contains NO
   Modal-based rename flow (the vehicle name is rendered via
   PageContainer's title string with no edit affordance). The backend
   also exposes no PATCH/PUT endpoint for vehicle metadata under
   /api/v1/vehicles/{id} — only GET, DELETE, /wake, /command etc.
   Wiring up rename would require both a new VehicleHeader edit
   affordance AND a new backend handler, which falls outside the
   prompt's allowed-files regex (frontend-only).

2. features/locations/components/GeofenceList.tsx does NOT exist —
   geofence rendering lives in web/src/features/maps/pages/GeofencesPage.tsx
   (single-page CRUD with inline list of cards). EditableText was
   adopted there on the per-card name span. The Pencil "edit details"
   button that opens the full Modal (lat/lng/radius/alerts) was
   intentionally LEFT in place — inline rename is a fast path, not a
   replacement for the multi-field editor.

3. features/notifications/components/AlertRuleList.tsx does NOT exist
   — the rule list lives in web/src/features/notifications/pages/AlertRulesPage.tsx.
   EditableText was adopted there on the rule name cell using the
   custom display render prop so the existing <Link to="/alert-studio?rule=ID">
   navigation affordance is preserved AND a sibling pencil button calls
   onStartEdit. We deliberately did NOT make double-click on the Link
   itself enter edit mode — single-click navigation fires before
   dblclick in every browser, which would make the affordance
   unusable in practice.

Allowlist regex used for the GIT_STATUS check (replaces the prompt's
default with the two adjusted file paths above):
  (components/ui/EditableText|components/ui/index|features/maps/pages/GeofencesPage|features/notifications/pages/AlertRulesPage|i18n/en|phase-46-38-inline-edit\.log)
